{
  "schema": 1,
  "verified": true,
  "retrieved": "2026-10-31",
  "what_this_is": "Soft-magnetic material constants and real core geometries, transcribed from the vendor pages named in every row's `source`. This is NOT a design rule: every number here is one vendor's published typical value at one condition, and the condition is stored with it.",
  "what_this_is_not": [
    "Not a Steinmetz fit. No vendor coefficients (Cm/x/y) were reachable in a form that could be quoted here, so every `steinmetz` field is null on purpose. magnetics_core_loss already takes the caller's k/alpha/beta, and select_core will only extrapolate a core loss away from a measured reference point when YOU supply the two exponents.",
    "Not a thermal model. No Rth (thermal resistance) was found for any part, so select_core reports watts and refuses a temperature rise.",
    "Not a B-H curve. `bsat` is one point (or two, if the vendor published two temperatures); the shape between the points, the DC-bias roll-off of AL, and the temperature coefficient of AL are all missing.",
    "Not every grade of every shape. The rows are the ones whose vendor page actually stated the numbers; absence is recorded as absence, not filled in."
  ],
  "unit_notes": {
    "ae_mm2": "effective cross-sectional area, mm^2 (vendor 'Ae')",
    "le_mm": "effective magnetic path length, mm (vendor 'le' / 'Lef')",
    "ve_mm3": "effective core volume, mm^3 (vendor 'Ve' / 'Vef')",
    "al_nh": "inductance factor, nH/turn^2, at the gap stated in `gap_um` (0 = ungapped). Vendor tolerance is in `al_tolerance_pct` where published.",
    "amin_mm2": "minimum cross-section (vendor 'Amin'), mm^2 - the flux density peak is bounded by THIS, not by Ae, in a core whose centre leg is narrower than the outer legs",
    "core_factor_mm1": "vendor 'C1' / 'sum(I/A)', 1/mm",
    "mass_g": "set mass (both halves for a two-piece core) unless `mass_basis` says otherwise",
    "loss_ref": "the ONE measured loss point the vendor published for this part, with its condition. f_khz is kilohertz - note that not every vendor measures at 100 kHz.",
    "aw_mm2": "usable winding area of the matching coil former, mm^2 (vendor 'winding area'). Only present where a former datasheet was reachable.",
    "mlt_mm": "mean length per turn for the matching coil former, mm (vendor 'average length of turn')"
  },
